 736, 1136], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"Totals may not equal the sum of components due to rounding.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1155, 854, 1183], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"The accompanying notes are an integral part of these financial statements.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1216, 896, 1242], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"1 Amounts represent changes between valuation dates 1/1/2011 and 1/1/2012.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 1242, 1455, 1294], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"2 Includes Railroad Retirement changes between valuation dates 1/1/2011 and 1/1/2012 and Black Lung changes between 9/30/2011 and 9/30/12.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1452, 94, 1495, 130], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"83\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [716, 127, 916, 158], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [386, 207, 1244, 255], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Airport and Airway Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 271, 792, 512], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"The Airport and Airway Trust Fund was established on the books of Treasury in fiscal year 1971, according to provisions of the Airport and Airway Revenue Act of 1970 [49 United States Code 1742(a), repealed]. The Tax Equity and Fiscal Responsibility Act of 1982 (Public Law 97-248, dated September 3, 1982) reestablished the trust fund in the Internal Revenue Code (26 United States Code 9502) effective September 1, 1982.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 514, 794, 761], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Treasury transfers from the general fund to the trust fund amounts equivalent to the taxes received from transportation of persons and property by air, gasoline and jet fuel used in commercial and noncommercial aircraft, and an international arrival and departure tax. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1990 (Public Law 101-508, dated November 5, 1990) increased rates for the excise taxes transferred to the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 761, 794, 849], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Treasury bases these transfers on estimates made by the Secretary of the Treasury. These are subject to adjustments in later transfers in the amount of actual tax receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 849, 796, 974], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"The FAA Modernization and Reform Act 2012 (Public Law 112-095), effective February 14, 2012, extended the aviation excise taxes until September 30, 2015. The Act included provisions that:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 981, 790, 1226], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Retained the existing passenger ticket, flight segment, and freight waybill taxes. The flight segment tax is indexed to the Consumer Price Index; effective calendar year 2014, the tax is $4.00. It also retained a special rule applied to flights between the continental United States and Alaska or Hawaii. This departure tax is indexed to the Consumer Price Index; effective calendar year 2014, the tax is $8.70.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 1235, 790, 1360], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Retained the existing tax per person for international flights that begin or end in the United States. The tax is indexed to the Consumer Price Index; effective calendar year 2014, the tax is $17.50.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 1362, 794, 1459], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Retained the existing tax on payments to airlines for frequent flyer and similar awards by banks and credit card companies, merchants and frequent flyer program\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 266, 1495, 332], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"partners, such as other airlines, hotels and rental car companies, and other businesses.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [842, 335, 1494, 401], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Retained the commercial aviation fuel tax and the general aviation jet fuel/gas taxes.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 403, 1494, 589], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Imposed a new surtax on fuel used in aircraft that is part of a fractional ownership program; the surtax applies to fuel used after March 31, 2012. It also changed the classification of transportation as part of a fractional ownership program from commercial aviation to noncommercial aviation.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 596, 1492, 750], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Repealed the excise tax exemption for transportation by small aircraft operating on nonestablished lines. (IRS defines the term \\\"operated on an established line\\\" to mean operated with some degree of regularity between definite points).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [842, 750, 1494, 969], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"When the provisions of 26 United States Code 9602(b) are met, amounts available in the trust fund exceed outlay requirements, Treasury invests excess amounts in public debt securities and credits the interest to the fund. Additional sums from the general fund also are credited as authorized and made available, by law, if they are needed to meet outlay requirements.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 971, 1497, 1179], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Treasury makes available to the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA), Department of Transportation (DOT), amounts required for outlays to carry out the Airport and Airway program. The Secretary of the Treasury makes other charges to the trust fund to transfer certain refunds of taxes and certain outfits, under section 34 of the Internal Revenue Code (IRC).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 1179, 1494, 1370], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress, required by 26 U.S.C. 9602 (a), are submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury, after consultation with the Secretary of Transportation. These reports are required to cover the financial condition and results of operations of the trust fund during the past fiscal year and those expected during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1370, 1989, 1494, 2015], \"page_id\": 86}], \"content\": \"March 2014\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 92, 177, 125], \"page_id\": 87}], \"content\": \"84\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [716, 94, 916, 130], \"page_id\": 87}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [475, 189, 1158, 276], \"page_id\": 87}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-1.\\u2014Airport and Airway Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [754, 273, 882, 304], \"page_id\": 87}], \"content\": \"[Source: DOT]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 309, 1492, 1146], \"pa