rd\": [534, 193, 1098, 231], \"page_id\": 99}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-6A.\\u2014Highway Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 238, 803, 431], \"page_id\": 99}], \"content\": \"The following information is released according to the provisions of the Byrd Amendment [codified at 26 United States Code 9503(d)] and represents data concerning the Highway Trust Fund. The figure described as \\\"unfunded authorizations\\\" is the latest estimate received from the DOT for fiscal year 2013.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [821, 240, 1497, 429], \"page_id\": 99}], \"content\": \"The 48-month revenue estimates for the highway and mass transit accounts, respectively, include the latest estimates received from Treasury's Office of Tax Analysis for excise taxes, net of refunds. They represent net highway receipts for those periods beginning at the close of fiscal year 2013.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [690, 509, 951, 554], \"page_id\": 99}], \"content\": \"Highway Account\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [692, 563, 945, 587], \"page_id\": 99}], \"content\": \"(In billions of dollars. Source: DOT)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 589, 1490, 952], \"page_id\": 99}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Commitments (unobligated balances plus unpaid obligations, fiscal year 2015)</td><td>90</td></tr><tr><td>less:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Cash balance (fiscal year 2015)</td><td>-10</td></tr><tr><td>Unfunded authorizations (fiscal year 2015)</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>48-month revenue estimate (fiscal years 2016, 2017, 2018, and 2019)</td><td>133</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [656, 1082, 974, 1120], \"page_id\": 99}], \"content\": \"Mass Transit Account\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [690, 1129, 953, 1155], \"page_id\": 99}], \"content\": \"[In billions of dollars. Source: DOT]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [148, 1157, 1494, 1516], \"page_id\": 99}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Commitments (unobligated balances plus unpaid obligations, fiscal year 2015)</td><td>25</td></tr><tr><td>less:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Cash balance (fiscal year 2015)</td><td>-2</td></tr><tr><td>Unfunded authorizations (fiscal year 2015)</td><td>27</td></tr><tr><td>48-month revenue estimate (fiscal years 2016, 2017, 2018, and 2019)</td><td>25</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 1537, 1202, 1563], \"page_id\": 99}], \"content\": \"Note.\\u2014Estimates are based on Fiscal Year 2015 President's Budget assumptions. Note.\\u2014Detail may not add to totals due to rounding.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 1987, 268, 2018], \"page_id\": 99}], \"content\": \"March 2014\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [714, 94, 918, 127], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1452, 94, 1497, 127], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"97\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [392, 207, 1242, 257], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Inland Waterways Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 266, 803, 578], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"The Inland Waterways Trust Fund was established by the Treasury in fiscal year 1984, pursuant to section 203 of the Inland Waterways Revenue Act of 1978 (Public Law 95-502) and continued pursuant to section 1405 of the Water Resources Development Act of 1986 (Public Law 99-662, codified at 26 United States Code 9506). Under 26 United States Code 9506(b), amounts from taxes on fuel used in commercial transportation on inland waterways, as determined by the Secretary of the Treasury, are appropriated to the trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [129, 573, 809, 799], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"The Technical and Miscellaneous Revenue Act of 1988 (Public Law 100-647, approved November 10, 1988) increased the tax each year, 1990 through 1995. These amounts are transferred quarterly from the general fund based on estimates made by the Secretary, subject to adjustments in later transfers to the amounts of actual tax receipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 266, 1497, 641], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"The Secretary of the Treasury invests in interest-bearing obligations of the United States that portion of the trust fund, in his judgment, not required to meet current withdrawals. The interest on, and proceeds from, the sale or redemption of any obligation held in the trust fund is credited to the trust fund. The Inland Waterways Revenue Act of 1978 (Public Law 95-502) provides that amounts in the trust fund shall be available as provided, by appropriations acts, for construction and rehabilitation expenditures for navigation on the inland and intracoastal waterways of the United States described in 33 United States Code 1804. Expenditures must be otherwise authorized by law.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 639, 1501, 820], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"Annual reports to Congress are required by 26 United States Code 9602(a) to be submitted by the Secretary of the Treasury. These reports are required to cover the financial condition and the results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and its expected condition and operations during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [486, 863, 1146, 948], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-7.\\u2014Inland Waterways Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [614, 955, 1016, 985], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"[Source: Department of the Army Corps of Engineers]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 983, 1497, 1275], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2012</td><td>$45,935,897</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fuel taxes/revenues</td><td>75,110,280</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>42,910</td></tr><tr><td>Gain on sale of investments</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>75,153,190</td></tr><tr><td>Transfers:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Corps of Engineers</td><td>86,167,807</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2013</td><td>$34,921,280</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [317, 1367, 1313, 1459], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"Inland Waterways Trust Fund\\nExpected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 2014-2018*\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [545, 1454, 1095, 1487], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars. Source: Department of the Army Corps of Engineers)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1485, 1497, 1796], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>2014</th><th>2015</th><th>2016</th><th>2017</th><th>2018</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>35</td><td>26</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>19</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fuel taxes</td><td>85</td><td>86</td><td>89</td><td>90</td><td>91</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>85</td><td>86</td><td>89</td><td>90</td><td>91</td></tr><tr><td>Transfers:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Corps of Engineers</td><td>94</td><td>92</td><td>90</td><td>90</td><td>90</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>26</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>19</td><td>20</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 1824, 809, 1890], \"page_id\": 100}], \"content\": \"* Outyear projections are based on economic conditions and agencies' best projections of revenues and expenditures.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 99, 173, 123], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"98\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [723, 99, 914, 123], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [280, 210, 1353, 250], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Leaking Underground Storage Tank Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 266, 803, 601], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"The Leaking Underground Storage Tank (LUST) Trust Fund was established in fiscal year 1981 according to provisions of the Comprehensive Environmental Response, Compensation and Liability Act of 1980 (Public Law 96-510, codified at 26 United States Code 9508), as amended by the Superfund Amendments and Re-authorization Act of 1986 (Public Law 99-499, dated October 17, 1986), sections 13163I and 13242(d)(42) of the Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1993 (Public Law 103-66, dated August 10, 1993), and section 1032(e)(13) of the Taxpayer Relief Act of 1987 (Public Law 105-34, dated August 5, 1997).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 603, 801, 695], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"The LUST Trust Fund is financed by taxes collected on gasoline, diesel fuels, special motor fuels, aviation fuels and fuels used in commercial transportation on inland\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 262, 1494, 417], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"waterways. Amounts available in the LUST Trust Fund, exceeding current expenditure requirements, are invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in interest-bearing Government securities (e.g., Treasury bills). All interest earned is credited directly to the LUST Trust Fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 420, 1494, 509], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"To carry out the LUST program, amounts are appropriated for the LUST Trust Fund to the EPA for programmatic and administrative expenses.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 514, 1497, 693], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"An annual report to Congress by the Secretary of the Treasury is required by 26 United States Code 9602(a). These reports present the financial condition of the LUST Trust Fund and results of operations for the past fiscal year and its expected condition and operations during the next 5 fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [413, 735, 1237, 806], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-8.\\u2014Leaking Underground Storage Tank Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2013\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [767, 811, 876, 834], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"[Source: EPA]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [157, 849, 1484, 1261], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2012</td><td>$1,157,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Taxes</td><td>162,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Interest</td><td>23,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Sequestered Resources<sup>2</sup></td><td>5,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Gross tax receipts</td><td>190,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Undisbursed balances:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Environmental Protection Agency Leaking Underground Storage Tank balances</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Total undisbursed balances</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Environmental Protection Agency Leaking Underground Storage Tank expenses</td><td>104,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Other expenses</td><td>3,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>$107,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2013</td><td>$1,240,000,000</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [158, 1301, 790, 1379], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"1 Reporting in this trust fund table is consistent with previously reported presentations. However, the structure of this table may not accurately reflect the status of this trust fund. As a result, this table may be revised in future reports and other resources should be utilized for accurate trust fund reporting.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 1301, 1461, 1344], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"2 Balances as of September 30, 2013 include the temporarily sequestered resources that came available with the appropriation on October 1, 2013.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [362, 1419, 1280, 1492], \"page_id\": 101}], \"content\": \"Leaking Underground Storage Tank Trust Fund Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 2014-2018\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [690, 1499, 954, 1520], \"page_id\": 101}], \"con